      "text": "🇧🇬 Iliana Yotova Wins Bulgaria's Presidential Election\n\nBulgaria's incumbent President Iliana Yotova has won today's runoff against pro-Western former caretaker Prime Minister Andrey Gyurov, according to parallel vote counts. Pollsters Alpha Research, Myara and Trend put her at 57% to 59%, with Myara and Trend giving Gyurov about 38%. Official results are expected within three days.\n\nYotova is not openly pro-Russian, but she favors dialogue with Moscow and opposes military aid to Ukraine. She said more weapons and money for Kiev only bring more destruction and deaths, and that peace can only come through negotiations that include Russia. She branded her opponents \"warmongers\" who want Russia to capitulate, and promised that no Bulgarian soldiers will go to Ukraine. She said she would speak to Putin if she had a mandate from the Bulgarian state and national consensus. AP expects her to back better relations with Russia and the lifting of sanctions, while keeping Bulgaria on its European path.\n\nYotova, who served as vice president under Rumen Radev, took over the presidency in January when he resigned to run in the snap parliamentary election. Radev, now prime minister and skeptical of support for Ukraine, backed her through his Progressive Bulgaria party, so the win keeps the presidency in the hands of the ruling majority.\n\nShe becomes the first woman directly elected as Bulgaria's president. Turnout was only about 29%, after a record low in the first round.\n\n🔴 @DDGeopolitics",
